      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Fulmentarus Terminator | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Fulmentarus Decurion | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 5 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
GUIDED WARHEADS When firing Frag missiles from their Cyclone Missile Launchers, Fulmentarus Terminators may fire at an enemy unit they cannot see if that unit is visible to a friendly model equipped with a Nuncio Vox. The Nuncio Vox bearer may not be embarked in a Vehicle, Falling Back, Pinned or engaged in close combat. Cyclone Missile Launchers firing in this manner: • Must use Frag missiles. • Count as Barrage weapons. • Follow the normal ProHammer rules for Barrage fire. Krak missiles may not use Guided Warheads.
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 5 Fulmentarus Terminators
Unit Type:
• Infantry
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Storm bolter
• Power fist
• Cyclone Missile Launcher
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Guided Warheads
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Fulmentarus Terminators for +65 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Power fist with:
• Chainfist ........................................ +5 points
• One Fulmentarus Terminator may be upgraded to:
• Fulmentarus Decurion ........................... +20 points
• The Fulmentarus Decurion may take:
• Grenade Harness ................................ +10 points
The Fulmentarus Decurion may select up to 50 points of permitted Terminator weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r8-um-ful-dt-transport-rule" name="Dedicated Transport" hidden="false"><description>This squad may select the listed Dedicated Transport where Transport Capacity permits.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-rule-0" name="Guided Warheads" hidden="false"><description>When firing Frag missiles from their Cyclone Missile Launchers, Fulmentarus Terminators may fire at an enemy unit they cannot see if that unit is visible to a friendly model equipped with a Nuncio Vox. The Nuncio Vox bearer may not be embarked, Falling Back, Pinned or engaged in close combat. These shots must use Frag missiles, count as Barrage and follow normal ProHammer Barrage rules. Krak missiles may not use Guided Warheads.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-rule-1" name="Wargear" hidden="false"><description>Cataphractii Terminator Armour; Storm bolter; Power fist; Cyclone Missile Launcher.</description></rule></rules>
