        <profile name="Marius Gage" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Marius Gage | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
• HQ
FIRST MASTER OF THE LEGION Friendly non-Vehicle Ultramarines units with at least one model within 12" of Marius Gage may use his Leadership characteristic when taking Morale or Pinning tests. MASTER OF ORGANISATION After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, select one Ultramarines Infantry unit which deployed normally. That unit may immediately be redeployed anywhere wholly within the Ultramarines deployment zone. All normal deployment restrictions must still be obeyed. The unit may not be placed into Reserve. Any Independent Characters already joined to the unit are redeployed with it. CALCULATED RESPONSE Marius Gage and any Ultramarines unit he has joined have Counter-Attack. COMMAND RETINUE Marius Gage may select a Legion Command Squad, Legion Terminator Command Squad or Invictarus Suzerain Squad as his retinue. The selected squad does not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot.
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Master-crafted Power Weapon
• Bolt pistol
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• First Master of the Legion
• Master of Organisation
• Calculated Response
OPTIONS
• Marius Gage may take:
• Krak grenades ................................... +2 points
• Melta bombs .................................... +5 points</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-rule-0" name="First Master of the Legion" hidden="false"><description>Friendly non-Vehicle Ultramarines units with at least one model within 12 inches of Marius Gage may use his Leadership for Morale or Pinning tests.

Pinning: Unsaved Wounds caused by this weapon force the unit to take a Pinning Test.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-rule-1" name="Master of Organisation" hidden="false"><description>After both armies deploy but before the first turn, select one Ultramarines Infantry unit which deployed normally. It may immediately redeploy wholly within the Ultramarines deployment zone, obeying all normal restrictions. It may not be placed into Reserve; joined Independent Characters redeploy with it.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-rule-2" name="Calculated Response" hidden="false"><description>Marius Gage and any Ultramarines unit he has joined have Counter-Attack.

Counter-Attack: If this unit is not engaged with any enemy models and an enemy unit successfully completes a charge move against it, the unit may take a Leadership test. If passed, this unit gains +1 Attack during the Assault phase.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-4-marius-gage-first-master-rule-3" name="Wargear" hidden="false"><description>Artificer Armour; Iron Halo; Master-crafted Power Weapon; Bolt pistol; Frag grenades.</description></rule></rules>
