            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+/5+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-6-aeonid-thiel-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Aeonid Thiel | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 3+/5+
One Legion Tactical Squad or Legion Veteran Squad may replace its Sergeant with Aeonid Thiel for +80 points. Thiel remains part of the squad for the entire battle. He is a Character but is not an Independent Character.
UNORTHODOX TACTICS After deployment but before the first turn begins, choose one of the following special rules: • Counter-Attack • Move Through Cover • Night Vision • Tank Hunters Thiel and every model in his squad gain the selected special rule for the duration of the battle. The unit retains the selected rule even if Thiel is subsequently slain.
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Refractor Field
• Power weapon
• Bolt pistol
• Purity Seals
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Unorthodox Tactics
If the squad purchases Krak grenades or Melta bombs,
Thiel receives the same upgrade at the normal squad cost.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
