      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Primarch of the Ultramarines, Lord of Ultramar, the Avenging Son
Roboute Guilliman was among the greatest commanders and statesmen of the Great Crusade, a Primarch whose genius lay not merely in winning battles, but in understanding the greater structure of war itself. Under his rule the worlds of Ultramar became a realm of extraordinary order and prosperity, while the XIII Legion grew into one of the largest and most disciplined forces of the Legiones Astartes.
Upon the battlefield Guilliman sought neither reckless glory nor rigid adherence to a single doctrine. Every engagement was studied, every success and failure considered, and theory was continually tested against the practical realities of war. His warriors were expected to adapt as swiftly as their Primarch, changing formation and method as circumstances demanded until the enemy was confronted with precisely the form of warfare it was least prepared to resist.
Roboute Guilliman | 7 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Roboute Guilliman
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Armour of Reason
• Gladius Incandor
• Hand of Dominion
• Arbitrator
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Master Strategist
• Preternatural Strategy
• Sire of Ultramar
• Theoretical / Practical
RESTRICTIONS
Roboute Guilliman may only be selected for a Loyalist Ultramarines army. He otherwise follows all normal rules and restrictions for Primarchs.
ARMOUR OF REASON A magnificent suit of war-plate fashioned according to the exacting requirements of the Primarch of the XIII Legion, the Armour of Reason combined formidable protection with the sophisticated command systems required to direct vast armies across the battlefield. The Armour of Reason counts as Primarch Armour. GLADIUS INCANDOR A superbly balanced blade wielded with the calculated precision that characterised Guilliman’s approach to war, Gladius Incandor was equally suited to the destruction of armoured warriors and monstrous foes. Gladius Incandor is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Shred special rule. HAND OF DOMINION A colossal powered gauntlet constructed for the strength of a Primarch, the Hand of Dominion could crush armour and tear apart even the heaviest engines of war. The Hand of Dominion is a Master-crafted Power Fist with the Armourbane special rule. ARBITRATOR Arbitrator was a master-crafted bolter fashioned to the proportions of the Primarch of the XIII Legion, capable of delivering exceptionally powerful and accurate fire. Weapon Range S AP Type Arbitrator 18" 6 3 Assault 2, Rending, Master-crafted MASTER STRATEGIST Few commanders possessed Guilliman’s ability to comprehend the flow of an entire battlefield and translate that understanding into precise orders. Unless a rule specifically states otherwise, the range of Roboute Guilliman’s special rules which affect friendly Ultramarines units is 18". PRETERNATURAL STRATEGY Guilliman’s ability to reassess a battle plan in moments allowed the XIII Legion to alter its dispositions even as the enemy committed itself to battle. After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, nominate one friendly Ultramarines unit. That unit may be redeployed anywhere it could legally have been deployed at the beginning of the battle. It must obey all normal deployment restrictions and may not be placed into Reserve unless it was already eligible to begin the battle in Reserve. SIRE OF ULTRAMAR The warriors of the XIII Legion fought beneath the gaze of a Primarch who demanded discipline in victory and adversity alike. Friendly Ultramarines units with at least one model within 12" of Roboute Guilliman may re-roll failed Morale tests. The second result must be accepted. THEORETICAL / PRACTICAL To Guilliman, no doctrine was valuable merely because it had succeeded before. Theory existed to be tested in battle, and practical experience existed to refine theory. At the beginning of each Ultramarines turn, choose one of the following doctrines. The chosen doctrine affects friendly Ultramarines units with at least one model within 18" of Roboute Guilliman until the beginning of the next Ultramarines turn. ADVANCE Affected units may move up to 1" further than normal during their Movement phase. FIRE Affected units may re-roll shooting To Hit rolls of 1. ASSAULT Affected units may re-roll close combat To Hit rolls of 1. PRIMARCH RETINUE Roboute Guilliman may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Invictarus Suzerain Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-0" name="Armour of Reason" hidden="false"><description>The Armour of Reason counts as Primarch Armour.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-1" name="Gladius Incandor" hidden="false"><description>Gladius Incandor is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks are resolved at +1 Strength and have Shred.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-2" name="Hand of Dominion" hidden="false"><description>The Hand of Dominion is a Master-crafted Power Fist with Armourbane.

Armourbane: Attack rolls 2D6 for Armour Penetration.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-3" name="Arbitrator" hidden="false"><description>Arbitrator: Range 18 inches, Strength 6, AP3, Assault 2, Rending, Master-crafted.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-4" name="Master Strategist" hidden="false"><description>Unless a rule specifically states otherwise, the range of Roboute Guilliman’s special rules which affect friendly Ultramarines units is 18 inches.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-5" name="Preternatural Strategy" hidden="false"><description>After both armies deploy but before the first turn, nominate one friendly Ultramarines unit. It may be redeployed anywhere it could legally have been deployed at the beginning of the battle, obeying all normal restrictions, and may not be placed into Reserve unless it was already eligible to begin there.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-6" name="Sire of Ultramar" hidden="false"><description>Friendly Ultramarines units with at least one model within 12 inches of Guilliman may re-roll failed Morale tests. The second result must be accepted.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-7" name="Theoretical / Practical" hidden="false"><description>At the beginning of each Ultramarines turn choose Advance, Fire or Assault. Until the next Ultramarines turn, friendly Ultramarines units within 18 inches gain respectively: +1 inch Movement; re-roll shooting To Hit rolls of 1; or re-roll close-combat To Hit rolls of 1.</description></rule><rule id="r8-r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-rule-8" name="Wargear" hidden="false"><description>Armour of Reason; Gladius Incandor; Hand of Dominion; Arbitrator; Frag Grenades.</description></rule></rules>
    <selectionEntryGroups><selectionEntryGroup id="r6-guilliman-retinue" name="Primarch Retinue — choose up to one (no additional FOC slot)" hidden="false"><constraints><constraint id="r6-guilliman-retinue-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><selectionEntries><selectionEntry type="unit" name="Legion Honour Guard Squad" id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-hq-praetor-ret-honour" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="55" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Standard Wargear" id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-hq-praetor-ret-honour-std" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every model wears Artificer Armour and carries a Refractor Field, Power Weapon, Bolt Pistol and Frag Grenades.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes" id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-hq-praetor-ret-honour-la" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every model has Legiones Astartes and And They Shall Know No Fear as presented in ProHammer Classic, and is not Fearless.

And They Shall Know No Fear: Automatically passes Regroup tests at the start of the turn and may be used normally for the rest of the turn. If caught by a pursuit, the unit automatically regroups and is re-engaged in close combat, and does not suffer extra wounds from being caught in a pursuit. Immune to Fear.
Fear: Enemy units in base contact must pass a Leadership test before resolving their close combat attacks. If the test fails, those units attack with WS1 in the melee engagement.
Fearless: Automatically passes all Morale and Pinning tests. May not Take Cover! or choose to voluntarily fail a break test.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Honour or Death" id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-hq-praetor-ret-honour-hod" hidden="false">
                  <description>If the Legion Champion is in base contact with one or more enemy Independent Characters, he must direct all of his close-combat attacks against one of them. When attacking an enemy Independent Character in close combat, he may re-roll failed To Hit and To Wound rolls.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Retinue" id="r6-guilliman-ret-0-hq-praetor-ret-honour-ret" hidden="false">
                  <description>Selected for an eligible Praetor or Primarch. It occupies no separate Force Organisation slot; the commander and Honour Guard count as a single HQ selection but do not have to deploy together and operate as separate units after deployment.</description>
                </rule>
